Alex: yo.
===

title: FirstMeeting
tags: meetingNight
---
???: ...
Ernest: !!
Ernest: Hello? Who are you?
???: ...
Ernest: My name is Ernest, what's yours?
???: It's dangerous out here. You should go back to your camp.
Ernest: Are you talking about the wolf?
???: Wolf? There are no wolves out here. I don't know what you're talking about.
Ernest: Oh..
Ernest: What are you doing out here anyway?
???: ... I live here.
Ernest: What? That's so cool! I've always wanted to live in the forest.
???: You can't tell anyone you saw me out here!
Ernest: I won't, I promise!
???:...
Alex: I'm Alex.
Ernest: It's nice to meet you, Alex.
Alex: ...
Ernest: You should join us at the camp. There's a warm fire, and sandwiches! 
Alex: I have everything I need out here.
Ernest: Are you sure?
Alex: Yes. 
Ernest: Oh.
Ernest: How long have you been out here? You can't have been living here forever. 
Alex: It's safer out here. People have never been kind to me.
Ernest: Oh. What about your parents?
Alex: I was separated from them a long time ago. I've been alone this whole time. I don't know where they are.
Ernest: I'm sorry. I couldn't imagine what it would be like if I didn't have my parents.
Alex: You swear you won't tell anybody you saw me out here? 
Ernest: I swear I won't.
Alex: Good.
Alex: ...
Alex: Why did you come out here anyway? 
Ernest: I've been so curious about the forest. I couldn't just leave here at the end of the week without seeing it for myself. 
Alex: There's nothing really exciting about it.
Ernest: What do you mean? I've found a new friend! 
Alex: Friend?
Ernest: If you want to be. You seem pretty friendly. 
Alex: I'm not friendly. 
Ernest: Oh…
Ernest: Would you mind if I brought you a sandwich tomorrow?
Alex: What?
Ernest: Aren't you hungry out here? Or do you eat berries?
Alex: ...
Alex: I suppose a sandwich could be nice. 
Ernest: Great! If you come to the same spot, I can meet you again tomorrow night.
Alex: Why would you want to come out every night just to see me? Shouldn't you be spending time at your camp?
Ernest: My friends at the camp, I enjoy their company. But it's always so loud. 
Ernest: I've always preferred the quiet, and to spend time alone.
Ernest: So I might as well come out here, where it's quiet.
Ernest: I've also never had a friend like me.
Alex: What do you mean? 
Ernest: You seem to enjoy the quiet. And you obviously spend a lot of time by yourself.
Alex: ... That's true.  
Alex: Still though, I think you should go back to your camp. It's getting late.
Ernest: You're right. I'll come see you tomorrow!
Alex: Ok... 
<<set $firstMeetingDone = true>>
===

title: SecondMeeting
tags: meetingNight
---
Alex: Ernest!!
Ernest: Ah! You scared me! 
Alex: Shh, keep it down. 
Ernest: You're the one who snuck up on me!
    -> Ernest: What are you doing here? 
    -> Ernest: How'd you get behind me? 
Alex: I have something I want to show you! Follow me. 
Ernest: What's this? 
Alex: I've been making these. There's some really nice looking leaves and sticks around here. If you collect them, you can make these cool patterns. 
Alex: You should try it for yourself! 
<<set $playLeaf = true>>
===

title: AfterLeaf
tags: meetingNight
---
Alex: Hey, those look pretty good! You're almost better than me.
Ernest: (thinking) His nails looked extra sharp when he was showing me those leaves. Were they like that yesterday? 
    -> Ask Alex about his nails.
        Ernest: Hey.. were your nails that long yesterday? They look extra sharp. 
        Alex: What do you expect me to cut my nails with? Does it look like I have any nail clippers around here? 
        Ernest: Oh… sorry. 
    -> Leave it alone.
        Ernest: (thinking) Maybe I just didn't get a good enough look at them... I shouldn't judge.  
Ernest: Where do you sleep each night? Surely you have somewhere to take shelter around here.
Alex: It's over those mountains, it's too far away for you to see. 
Alex: You can't stray too far from your camp.
Ernest: You're right. I should probably be getting back anyways, it's late. 
Ernest: I'll see you tomorrow though, right?
Alex: Yes, I'll be here. 


===

title: AfterSpotlight
tags: meetingNight
---
Ernest: What are you doing here?? You'll be seen.
Alex: It's fine, everyone is asleep, you were taking too long, I had to come see what was the hold up. 
Ernest: Well I was just about to leave before you came over here. Let's go before anyone hears us.
<<set $goToForestDay4 = true>>
===

title: InForestDay4
tags: meetingNight
---
Alex.: ...
Ernest: (thinking) Hmm.. were Alex's eyes always glowing like that? 
    -> Ask Alex about his eyes 
        Ernest: Hey, were your eyes always that bright?
        Alex.: What do you mean? 
        Ernest: Your eyes, they're almost glowing bright red!
        Alex.: I don't know what you're talking about. It's probably just the lighting. 
        Alex: See?
        Ernest: Maybe you're right, the moon is shining quite brightly tonight. 
    -> Don't mention it 
        Ernest: (thinking) It's probably just the lighting. The moon is shining quite brightly tonight. 
Ernest: I took some pictures today! There's a lot of nice flowers around the camp. 
Alex: Huh, those look pretty good. Maybe you could become a photographer.
Ernest: I've never thought about a job. I've kind of always just wanted to live in nature. 
Alex: Photography would let you spend all your time in nature!
Ernest: You're right! Then I could come see you in my travels! 
Alex: Don't take any pictures of me, though.
Ernest: Why not?
Alex: I wouldn't be much of a secret if there's photographic evidence of me. 
Ernest: Oh, good point. 
Ernest: How am I going to remember you after I go back home? 
Alex: I'll still be here, most likely. You can come visit me when you're older. 
Ernest: But that's ages away! How will I know you'll still be here? 
Alex: I don't really have anywhere else to go. 
Ernest: Why don't you live with me? When we leave tomorrow you can come with us on the bus. I've always wanted siblings. I'm sure my parents would be happy to have you. 
Alex: No, they would hate me. Everyone hates me. 
Alex: It's already been made clear to me that I'm not welcome anywhere. I promised myself not to go out into public ever again. 
Ernest: Did something happen? 
Alex: No one treats me kindly. It's safer out here. 
Ernest: ...
Ernest: I'll make sure to visit you as soon as possible. 
===

title: FinalMeeting
tags: reveal
---
<<set $playRevealAnim = true>>
Ernest: Alex, is that you?
Ernest: ...
<<jump FinalMeeting2>>
===

title: FinalMeeting2
---
<<set $hasSnuckOut = true>>
Ernest: It's been you this whole time, hasn't it?
Ernest: You're the wolf from the story? 
Ernest: You aren't going to hurt me, are you? You're my friend
Ernest: The signs were there the whole time. 
Ernest: I won't tell anyone about you, I promise. 
Ernest: You will be alright here. 
Ernest: You are where you belong, in the woods, free from any harm from people.
Ernest: I promise I'll return in the future, okay? Wait for me here. 
===